concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-6-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "474(7) 6  Interference with facilities"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-474-6-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against subsection (5) if:  (a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement officer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in good faith in the course of his or her duties; and  (b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances for the purpose of performing that duty. Note 1: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see subsection 13.3(3). Note 2: See also subsection 475.1(2) for the interaction between this defence and the Radiocommunications Act 1992." ;
    skos:definition "(7) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against subsection (5) if:  (a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement officer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in good faith in the course of his or her duties; and  (b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances for the purpose of performing that duty. Note 1: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see subsection 13.3(3). Note 2: See also subsection 475.1(2) for the interaction between this defence and the Radiocommunications Act 1992."@en ;
