concept:act-sch-1-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004  (a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement officer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the course of his or her duties; and  (b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances for the purpose of performing that duty. Note 1: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see subsection 13.3(3). Note 2: This subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against subsection (1) or (2) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that requires a warrant under some other law." ;
    skos:definition "Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004  (a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement officer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the course of his or her duties; and  (b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances for the purpose of performing that duty. Note 1: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see subsection 13.3(3). Note 2: This subsection merely creates a defence to an offence against subsection (1) or (2) and does not operate to authorise any conduct that requires a warrant under some other law."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6b7e72be623d6cdf49314f0484eabf47ab4e797ec46f0ec44fd2421bc5c01ec1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defence for law enforcement or intelligence officers acting in the course of their duties." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.26" ;
