    values:originalText "(2) A person (the first person) is guilty of an offence if:  (a) the first person uses a carriage service to make to another person (the second person) a threat to cause serious harm to the second person or a third person; and  (b) the first person intends the second person to fear that the threat will be carried out. Penalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.  Telecommunications offences  Schedule 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    25 Actual fear not necessary" ;
