concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-17 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "474 17  Using a carriage service to menace, harass or cause offence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-474-17 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:  (a) the person uses a carriage service; and  (b) the person does so in a way (whether by the method of use or the content of a communication, or both) that reasonable persons would regard as being, in all the circumstances, menacing, harassing or offensive. Penalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), that subsection applies to menacing, harassing or causing offence to:  (a) an employee of the NRS provider; or  (b) an emergency call person; or  (c) an employee of an emergency service organisation; or  Telecommunications offences  Schedule 1" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person is guilty of an offence if:  (a) the person uses a carriage service; and  (b) the person does so in a way (whether by the method of use or the content of a communication, or both) that reasonable persons would regard as being, in all the circumstances, menacing, harassing or offensive. Penalty: Imprisonment for 3 years.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), that subsection applies to menacing, harassing or causing offence to:  (a) an employee of the NRS provider; or  (b) an emergency call person; or  (c) an employee of an emergency service organisation; or  Telecommunications offences  Schedule 1"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a02f74bc19bcd38c4570e80c3e76ebad52b7d30033db76d9173d1ebde0544e86" ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-17-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-17-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
