concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-26 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "474 23 (possessing etc. child abuse material for use through a"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-474-26 ;
    values:originalText "carriage service) if:  (a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement officer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the course of his or her duties; and  (b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances for the purpose of performing that duty. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see subsection 13.3(3).  (4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against section 474.22 (using a carriage service for child abuse material) or" ;
    skos:definition "carriage service) if:  (a) the person is, at the time of the offence, a law enforcement officer, or an intelligence or security officer, acting in the course of his or her duties; and  (b) the conduct of the person is reasonable in the circumstances for the purpose of performing that duty. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection, see subsection 13.3(3).  (4) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against section 474.22 (using a carriage service for child abuse material) or"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a8fbdd4f9d941e86c9a3f18ee21ea6a55a150a120acf4789f525445ee3ffa8f1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "37"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Law enforcement and intelligence officers are not criminally responsible for possessing child abuse material if it is reasonable in the circumstances for their duty." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
