    skos:definition "(1) A person (the sender) commits an offence if:  (a) the sender uses a carriage service to transmit a communication to another person (the recipient); and  (b) the communication includes material that is indecent; and  (c) the sender does this with the intention of making it easier to procure the recipient to engage in, or submit to, sexual activity with the sender; and  (d) the recipient is someone who is, or who the sender believes to be, under 16 years of age; and  (e) the sender is at least 18 years of age. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 years."@en ;
