concept:act-sch-1-sec-474-36 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "474 30  Defences for NRS employees and emergency call persons"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-474-36 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against a provision of this Subdivision in relation to particular conduct if the person:  (a) is an employee of the NRS provider; and  (b) engages in the conduct in good faith in the course of the person’s duties as such an employee.  (2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against a provision of this Subdivision in relation to particular conduct if the person:  (a) is an emergency call person; and  (b) engages in the conduct in good faith in the course of the person’s duties as such an emergency call person." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against a provision of this Subdivision in relation to particular conduct if the person:  (a) is an employee of the NRS provider; and  (b) engages in the conduct in good faith in the course of the person’s duties as such an employee.  (2) A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against a provision of this Subdivision in relation to particular conduct if the person:  (a) is an emergency call person; and  (b) engages in the conduct in good faith in the course of the person’s duties as such an emergency call person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b24e2a069d92511cf205d3509ab994805a12f56a8666988f59d2a5824d6d3cf9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer ;
