concept:act-sch-2-sec-380-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "380 2  Contaminating goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-380-2 ;
    values:originalText "Offence based on implied nationhood power  (1) A person is guilty of an offence if:  (a) the person contaminates goods; and  (b) the person does so with intent:  (i) to cause public alarm or anxiety in Australia; or  (ii) to cause widespread, or nationally significant, economic loss in Australia through public awareness of the contamination, or possible contamination, of the goods; or  (iii) to cause harm to, or create a risk of harm to, public health in Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years. Offences based on other constitutional powers  (2) A person is guilty of an offence if:  (a) the person contaminates goods; and  (b) the person does so with intent to cause:  (i) public alarm or anxiety; or  (ii) economic loss through public awareness of the contamination, or possible contamination, of the goods; and  (c) any of the following subparagraphs applies:  (i) the loss is a loss to a constitutional corporation (other than a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution);  (ii) the loss is a loss to a constitutional corporation that is a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (iii) the goods belong to a constitutional corporation (other than a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution);  Contamination offence  Schedule 2  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    49  (iv) the goods belong to a constitutional corporation that is a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (v) the person is a constitutional corporation (other than a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution);  (vi) the person is a constitutional corporation that is a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (vii) the loss takes the form of detriment to constitutional trade and commerce;  (viii) the goods are in the course of, or intended for, constitutional trade and commerce;  (ix) the contamination occurs outside Australia and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (x) the loss is a loss to the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (3) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (2)(c)." ;
    skos:definition "Offence based on implied nationhood power  (1) A person is guilty of an offence if:  (a) the person contaminates goods; and  (b) the person does so with intent:  (i) to cause public alarm or anxiety in Australia; or  (ii) to cause widespread, or nationally significant, economic loss in Australia through public awareness of the contamination, or possible contamination, of the goods; or  (iii) to cause harm to, or create a risk of harm to, public health in Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years. Offences based on other constitutional powers  (2) A person is guilty of an offence if:  (a) the person contaminates goods; and  (b) the person does so with intent to cause:  (i) public alarm or anxiety; or  (ii) economic loss through public awareness of the contamination, or possible contamination, of the goods; and  (c) any of the following subparagraphs applies:  (i) the loss is a loss to a constitutional corporation (other than a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution);  (ii) the loss is a loss to a constitutional corporation that is a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (iii) the goods belong to a constitutional corporation (other than a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution);  Contamination offence  Schedule 2  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    49  (iv) the goods belong to a constitutional corporation that is a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (v) the person is a constitutional corporation (other than a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution);  (vi) the person is a constitutional corporation"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4a16ca5216bb976874328d9b257964bc13c22cacddc6f5ff1637b38ff5c03743" ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-380-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-380-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-2-sec-380-2-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.54" .
