commerce;  (viii) the goods are in the course of, or intended for, constitutional trade and commerce;  (ix) the person makes the statement in Australia using a postal or other like service or an electronic communication;  (x) the person makes the statement outside Australia and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (xi) the loss is a loss to the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority;  (xii) the statement is made to the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (3) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (2)(d).  (4) For the purposes of this section, making a statement includes conveying information by any means." ;
