    values:originalText "(2) A person is guilty of an offence if:  (a) the person makes a statement that the person believes to be false; and  (b) the person does so with the intention of inducing the person to whom the statement is made or others to believe that goods have been contaminated; and  (c) the person does so with intent to cause:  (i) public alarm or anxiety; or  (ii) economic loss through public awareness of the contamination, or possible contamination, of the goods; and  (d) any of the following subparagraphs applies:  (i) the loss is a loss to a constitutional corporation (other than a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution);  (ii) the loss is a loss to a constitutional corporation that is a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (iii) the goods belong to a constitutional corporation (other than a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution);  (iv) the goods belong to a constitutional corporation that is a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (v) the person is a constitutional corporation (other than a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution);  (vi) the person is a constitutional corporation that is a foreign corporation within the meaning of paragraph 51(xx) of the Constitution and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  Contamination offence  Schedule 2  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Offences and Other Measures) Act (No. 2) 2004                    53  (vii) the loss takes the form of detriment to constitutional trade and commerce;  (viii) the goods are in the course of, or intended for, constitutional trade and commerce;  (ix) the person makes the statement in Australia using a postal or other like service or an electronic communication;  (x) the person makes the statement outside Australia and the goods have been produced, manufactured, assembled or otherwise processed in Australia;  (xi) the loss is a loss to the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority;  (xii) the statement is made to the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years." ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer .

